WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.860
Speaker 1: Let's go to Richard from Jersey.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:05.740
Richard, welcome to the program.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:07.790
Speaker 2: Hello, David.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:09.599
Pleasure to be speaking with you.

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:11.679
Speaker 1: The pleasure is all mine.

00:00:11.679 --> 00:00:19.940
Speaker 2: So the thing on my mind right now,
I think the thing on a lot of people's mind

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.810
right now is just thinking ahead to the 2024
election.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:28.840
And it seems to me that the writing's on the
wall that long distance us is more than likely

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.840
going to be the Republican nomination.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.890
And I keep thinking about the prospect of
I didn't think of this.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:40.510
And it seems to me like we're.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:42.780
Speaker 1: Starting to lose you.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.250
The audio wasn't great to start with.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:50.030
It started at like a six and a half, but you're
quite literally just fading and cutting out

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:51.030
now.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:55.410
So I heard you say you think DeSantis will
be the nominee for the Republicans?

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.410
It's certainly possible.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:57.410
I don't know yet.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:58.780
It's too early for me to say that.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.739
You were then starting to talk about Biden,
and I just couldn't hear a word you were saying.

00:01:02.739 --> 00:01:03.760
Speaker 2: Okay.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:04.790
Does that sound.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:05.810
Speaker 1: Better?

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:06.840
Yes, it does.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:07.860
Speaker 2: Beautiful.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:16.550
So my main thing is I don't think Biden is
going to win against Ron DeSantis, but it's

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:21.600
he's still toting the line of saying that
he is going to run.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.170
And the more time that goes on, it seems that
he's going to.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:32.420
So I'm wondering what your thoughts are on
is it possible for him to change vice presidency

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.049
choice because Kamala Harris herself isn't
very popular either.

00:01:37.049 --> 00:01:44.430
Is it possible to get a more exciting, younger,
progressive candidate on the ticket with him

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.520
that could possibly bolster his chances?

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.740
Speaker 1: Okay, this is a good question.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:54.530
If Biden runs, could he and should he replace
Kamala Harris, his current VP, with someone

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:55.530
else?

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.090
He absolutely could.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:03.289
I think the problem with that is whatever
benefit Biden might get from, as you say,

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:10.400
a more exciting or likable VP running mate
in 24 could very easily be canceled out by

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:18.160
the fact that bailing on your VP for consecutive
terms might be seen as a sign of trouble in

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.129
paradise, for lack of a better term.

00:02:20.129 --> 00:02:22.780
So I don't know if I were advising Biden that.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:23.790
I would say to do that.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.120
I think you want to project stability.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.440
You want to project a steady hand.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:31.269
And part of that would be this.

00:02:31.269 --> 00:02:32.910
This is a good team.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:37.350
And even if people they're changing behind
the scenes, you go with that with the person

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:38.930
who is currently VP.

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:44.440
Also, it would be very strange and difficult
and awkward to be campaigning for several

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:49.120
months while Kamala Harris is still president
with somebody else as the running mate.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:53.070
I think it raises I think it creates problems
for Biden to do that.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.370
Speaker 2: Okay.

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:59.209
I take your point that it would be awkward,
but.

00:02:59.209 --> 00:03:02.569
My main thing with Biden, as always, is that
he's very low energy.

00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:07.440
And even though we were able to get past the
midterms pretty well, I think it would have

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:13.040
been better if we had had a president and
a vice president that inspires people to vote

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:18.220
for something instead of voting against the
greater evil.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:24.020
And I just I'm looking for things that Democrats
can do to do that for younger voters.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.690
And, you know, voters in general.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.440
Speaker 1: I agree with you generally.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:31.730
I don't know that replacing Kamala is that
thing, but I appreciate the idea.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.170
Speaker 2: Fair enough.

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:34.520
Thanks for speaking with me, David.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.520
Speaker 1: All right.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:36.520
Thank you for calling in.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:37.549
That's Richard from Jersey.

00:03:37.549 --> 00:03:40.510
Very, very powerful declarations there.

